# See https://citation-file-format.github.io/ for the full schema.
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AfriPlaybook in your research or work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AfriPlaybook: A Practical Guide to Building High-Quality Datasets for African Languages"
abstract: >
  An open, community-written guide to building high-quality datasets for
  African languages. It follows a dataset from first idea to public release:
  deciding what to collect and from whom, designing the annotation task,
  recruiting and paying annotators, checking their work, documenting the
  result, and publishing it so that others can build on it.
authors:
  - name: "Waraka Community"
    website: "https://waraka.org/"
url: "https://afriplaybook.waraka.org/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/warakacommunity/playbook"
date-released: "2026-04-30"
keywords:
  - "African languages"
  - "natural language processing"
  - "low-resource NLP"
  - "dataset annotation"
  - "machine translation"
  - "Masakhane"
license: MIT
